; Windows installer customisation (ADR 0049 §1–§3, decided in [O13]): the installer ships only the shell, the UI, bun.exe
; and aria2c.exe; the rest of the toolchain is downloaded on first run. This file does three things:
;
;   1. Asks — once, in the wizard — whether the future tool directories should be put on the *user* PATH (HKCU, no
;      administrator rights), defaulting to yes, and records the answer so uninstall can remove exactly those entries again.
;   2. Maintenance: running the installer again over an installed copy asks what to do (uninstall, reinstall, and upgrade when
;      this installer is newer). Uninstall starts the installed uninstaller; it is the only way in besides "Apps & features".
;   3. Uninstall: a page lets the user keep the toolchain, the CLI and/or the data; the sign-in credentials are always removed.
;
; Security and correctness notes:
;   - The registry work is done by build/win-path.ps1 (run through nsExec), not by NSIS's registry plugin. NSIS strings are
;     too short for a large PATH, and a partial write would truncate the user's PATH; the script reads and writes the whole
;     value, keeps REG_EXPAND_SZ, and refuses (without writing) above 30 000 characters.
;   - File removal is done by build/win-uninstall.ps1: NSIS's RMDir /r fails on the long paths of a Rust or Python tree and
;     follows links; the script removes a link as a link and checks every target is under the user's profile.
;   - The PATH page and the maintenance page are skipped on an update (${isUpdated}); an update must not re-ask, re-add or
;     remove anything, and the old uninstaller that an update runs is told `--updated`, which keeps all user state.
;   - Silent fresh installs keep the default (checked), as no page is shown. A silent uninstall removes everything unless told
;     otherwise: `--keep-tools`, `--keep-cli`, `--keep-data` (the credentials still go).
;
; Included before installer.nsi's own MUI2 include by electron-builder's NSIS header, so pull MUI2 in here first.
!include "MUI2.nsh"
!include "LogicLib.nsh"
!include "nsDialogs.nsh"

!ifndef CGS_INSTALLER_NSH
!define CGS_INSTALLER_NSH

; electron-builder's NSIS 3.0.4.1 has no ${NSD_CreateFirstRadioButton} (3.0.5+ does); same definition as upstream's.
!ifndef __NSD_FirstRadioButton_CLASS
  !define __NSD_FirstRadioButton_CLASS ${__NSD_RadioButton_CLASS}
  !define __NSD_FirstRadioButton_STYLE ${DEFAULT_STYLES}|${WS_TABSTOP}|${WS_GROUP}|${BS_TEXT}|${BS_VCENTER}|${BS_AUTORADIOBUTTON}|${BS_MULTILINE}
  !define __NSD_FirstRadioButton_EXSTYLE ${__NSD_RadioButton_EXSTYLE}
  !insertmacro __NSD_DefineControl FirstRadioButton
!endif

; Generated by scripts/fetch-win-bundle.mjs from desktop/toolchain/layout.json.
!include "${BUILD_RESOURCES_DIR}\win-bundle\userpaths.nsh"

; The folders under %APPDATA% that are the app's own data: Electron's userData is named after the product name from
; package.json (electron-builder's own removal only knows the file-name form, which is "cgs-desktop" here), its caches after
; the package name. The helper ignores duplicates.
!define CGS_APPDATA_NAMES "${PRODUCT_NAME};${PRODUCT_FILENAME};${APP_FILENAME};${APP_PACKAGE_NAME}"

!ifndef BUILD_UNINSTALLER
Var cgsAddToPath
Var cgsPathCheckbox
Var cgsIsUpdate
; Maintenance: what is installed, how this installer relates to it, and what the user chose.
Var cgsInstalledVersion
Var cgsUninstallString
Var cgsRelation
Var cgsMode
Var cgsRadio1
Var cgsRadio2
Var cgsRadio3
Var cgsAction1
Var cgsAction2
Var cgsAction3
!else
Var cgsRmTools
Var cgsRmCli
Var cgsRmData
Var cgsToolsBox
Var cgsCliBox
Var cgsDataBox
!endif
Var cgsPathHelperDir
Var cgsPathHelper
Var cgsUninstallHelper

LangString CGS_PATH_TITLE 1033 "CGS tools"
LangString CGS_PATH_TITLE 2052 "CGS 工具"
LangString CGS_PATH_SUBTITLE 1033 "Choose whether the tools go on your user PATH"
LangString CGS_PATH_SUBTITLE 2052 "选择是否把工具加入你的用户 PATH"
LangString CGS_PATH_INTRO 1033 "CGS Desktop downloads Git, Python, clang, Rust and the language servers on first run.$\r$\n$\r$\nAdding their directories to your user PATH lets you use them in your own terminals. This changes only your account and needs no administrator rights."
LangString CGS_PATH_INTRO 2052 "CGS Desktop 会在首次运行时下载 Git、Python、clang、Rust 与语言服务器。$\r$\n$\r$\n把它们的目录加入你的用户 PATH 后，你可以在自己的终端里直接使用这些工具。这只修改你的账户，不需要管理员权限。"
LangString CGS_PATH_CHECK 1033 "Add the CGS tools to my user PATH (no administrator rights needed)"
LangString CGS_PATH_CHECK 2052 "将 CGS 工具加入我的用户 PATH（不需要管理员权限）"
LangString CGS_PATH_HINT 1033 "If you leave this unticked, the desktop app and the agents it starts still find the tools; only your own terminals will not."
LangString CGS_PATH_HINT 2052 "取消勾选时，桌面应用及其启动的 agent 仍然能找到这些工具，只是你自己的终端找不到。"

LangString CGS_MAINT_TITLE 1033 "CGS Desktop is already installed"
